<title>INDIA: Indian castor trade shut for religious festival.</title>
<headline>Indian castor trade shut for religious festival.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's castor markets remained shut on Tuesday, after Monday's closure, both for local religious festivals. They reopen on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>On the last trading day on Friday, castor prices fell marginally on profit-taking by traders and dealers said they expected the market to slide further. &quot;Technically the market is overbought and may attract further correction,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
